[META]
framework: claude-framework
file_id: backlog.SYNC
class: universal
version: 1.0.0

[SYNC]
overview: Explicit synchronization between the local backlog and an external tracker (Azure DevOps, Linear, GitHub Issues)
principle: Sync is ALWAYS manual. Agent never silently pushes or pulls. Duplication between local and external is accepted; resolution is by explicit user instruction.

[WHY_EXPLICIT_ONLY]
Silent sync causes two failure modes:
  1. Agent overwrites external edits a human made (teammate updates the ticket; sync clobbers)
  2. Agent pollutes the tracker with experimental items that were never meant to leave the repo

Both are hard to undo and erode trust in the tracker. Explicit sync keeps the user in control of both direction and timing.

[PROJECT_POLICY]
# OpenGL Engine: GitHub Issues (Prorok1015/OpenGL_Engine) is the PRIMARY tracker (sync_target: github).
primary_tracker: GitHub Issues — epics (label epic, native sub-issues), stories (label story, one per US-NN-X), bugs (label bug)
milestones: 1 «Фаза 0 — этап C», 2 «Фаза 0 — этап D», 3 «M1 Проект и игровой модуль», 4 «M2 Данные», 5 «M3 Документный редактор», 6 «M4 Runtime», 7 «M5 Игровой UI», 8 «M6 Выпуск этапа А», 9 «Этап Б (ТЗ)»
local_backlog_role: short-lived scratch for follow-ups found mid-session; anything that outlives the session is pushed to GitHub Issues (SYNC_PUSH) and the BL item is archived with a link
commits: reference the issue — `refs #N` while working, `closes #N` in the commit that completes it
manifest: docs/agent/tracker/manifest.json mirrors the initial issue set (key → number); new issues need not be added there

[SUPPORTED_TARGETS]
Set INDEX.toon [BACKLOG_META].sync_target to one of:
  - none           — no sync available; ignore SYNC operations (default)
  - azure-devops   — via the Azure DevOps MCP server or REST API
  - linear         — via Linear MCP server
  - github         — via `gh` CLI or GitHub MCP server

Other trackers can be added by extending this file in a future release.

[CONFIGURATION_FIELDS]
These live in INDEX.toon [BACKLOG_META] and are set at SETUP or by user command:
  - sync_target: <one of above>
  - sync_project: <tracker-specific project id/name, e.g. "MyOrg/MyProj" for Azure DevOps>
  - sync_default_area: <optional, where new items go by default>
  - sync_default_type: <optional, tracker-specific work item type mapping>

The agent MUST NOT store credentials in these files. Credentials come from the environment or MCP config.

[SYNC_OPERATIONS]

[SYNC_PUSH]
purpose: Create or update external items to match local state
triggered_by: User says "push BL-042" / "sync to Azure DevOps" / "export the backlog"
steps:
  1. Read items/<id>.toon
  2. If [LINKS].external_id is empty → CREATE in external tracker; capture returned external_id
  3. If non-empty → UPDATE the referenced external item
  4. Map fields per mapping table below
  5. Write returned external_id back to items/<id>.toon [LINKS].external_id
  6. Append HISTORY line: "<ISO> — sync push → <tracker>:<external_id>"
safety:
  - Always show the user what will be pushed BEFORE making the API call
  - On create, confirm the target project/area
  - On update, show diff of what the push would change externally

[SYNC_PULL]
purpose: Update local items from external state
triggered_by: User says "pull BL-042" / "refresh from Linear"
steps:
  1. Read items/<id>.toon → get [LINKS].external_id
  2. Fetch current state from tracker
  3. Show diff between local and external
  4. Ask user per-field which side wins — do NOT auto-merge
  5. Apply resolved values; append HISTORY line: "<ISO> — sync pull <- <tracker>:<external_id> — fields updated: <list>"

[SYNC_LINK]
purpose: Associate an existing local item with an existing external item (no creation)
triggered_by: User says "link BL-042 to AB#1234"
steps:
  1. Fetch external item to confirm it exists and is accessible
  2. Write [LINKS].external_id
  3. Append HISTORY line: "<ISO> — linked to <tracker>:<external_id>"
no_fields_are_copied: Linking is just a reference; use SYNC_PULL to bring fields across

[SYNC_CAPTURE]
purpose: Create a local item FROM an external one (inverse of SYNC_PUSH)
triggered_by: User says "capture AB#1234 into the backlog"
steps:
  1. Fetch external item
  2. Run OP_ADD (see OPERATIONS.toon) with fields mapped from external
  3. Set [LINKS].external_id to the source
  4. Status defaults to `accepted` (already exists externally; presumed reviewed)

[FIELD_MAPPING_TABLE]
# Default mappings; projects may override by adding a [SYNC_FIELD_OVERRIDES] block in INDEX.toon.
#
# local field     → azure-devops           linear             github
# title           → System.Title           title              title
# type            → work item type         label:type:<type>  label:type:<type>
# status          → System.State           state              state (open/closed) + label
# priority        → Microsoft.VSTS.Common.Priority  priority   label:priority:<P>
# description     → System.Description     description        body (section)
# motivation      → (append to desc)       (append to desc)   body (section)
# acceptance      → System.AcceptanceCriteria  (append to desc)  body (section)
# theme           → area path              label:theme:<v>    label:theme:<v>

[STATUS_MAPPING]
# Map local status ↔ external state. Agent reads/writes via this mapping.
#
# local          azure-devops      linear              github
# proposed       New               Backlog             open + label:backlog
# accepted       Approved          Todo                open + label:accepted
# in-progress    Active            In Progress         open + label:in-progress
# done           Closed (Done)     Done                closed + label:done
# deferred       New + tag:deferred  Backlog + tag:deferred  open + label:deferred
# rejected       Removed           Canceled            closed + label:wontfix

[CONFLICT_RULES]
When local and external disagree (detected during SYNC_PULL):
  - Never auto-merge
  - Show user a side-by-side diff per field
  - Default proposal: external wins for `status`; local wins for `description/motivation/acceptance` (these are agent's working notes, not the external source of truth)
  - User can override any field choice; agent respects user's decision and writes HISTORY line explaining it

[BULK_SYNC_RULES]
Bulk operations ("sync all open items") require extra care:
  - Present a plan of what will push / pull / conflict BEFORE doing anything
  - Get explicit approval for the batch
  - If ANY item in the batch fails mid-way → stop, report progress, ask whether to retry or abort
  - Never exceed 10 API calls per minute to the external tracker; throttle if needed
